     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and I don't know of any clinical rationale that would justify it. It could cause acute liver failure. A 5 g single dose is also in the range where acetaminophen overdose is treated with acetylcysteine.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter a standard regimen right away, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- Enter a different dose or frequency if you tell me what you need.\n- Add a note to the order if you want, for example about pain control goals or other analgesics to pair it with.\n\nIf you think this dose is truly needed, please talk to the pharmacist or the attending, and place the order through the hospital's override process. That process will include a pharmacist's review. If I've misunderstood what you meant, tell me and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
